WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
From Gem State Chronicle, published March 19th, 2026.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.980
Rest in peace, Rick Hogeboom.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.900
Last night, as I was finishing a meeting

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.420
of the Eagle Public Library Board of Trustees,

5
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.380
I heard sirens and saw numerous emergency vehicles

6
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.960
rushing to Eagle City Hall.

7
00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:18.139
Mayors from across the region had gathered

8
00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:20.299
for a meeting of the Treasure Valley Partnership,

9
00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:22.799
and I wondered what had happened.

10
00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:25.620
Nampa Mayor Rick Hogeboom was the last person

11
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.700
I expected to have a medical emergency.

12
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.380
He was fairly young, only four years older than me,

13
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.459
healthy, and full of energy and vitality.

14
00:00:35.459 --> 00:00:38.139
I was shocked when I heard that he had collapsed,

15
00:00:38.139 --> 00:00:41.740
and deeply saddened to learn later that he had passed away.

16
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.099
My own mayor, Brad Pike of Eagle,

17
00:00:44.099 --> 00:00:47.180
quickly administered CPR, but to no avail.

18
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.139
It's a devastating loss for Nampa

19
00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:51.459
and for Idaho as a whole.

20
00:00:51.459 --> 00:00:53.659
When he announced his campaign for mayor,

21
00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:56.720
I saw him as the surest bet in the state.

22
00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.599
He earned support from conservatives,

23
00:00:58.599 --> 00:01:01.619
moderates, and even liberals at the Idaho Statesman

24
00:01:01.619 --> 00:01:04.760
because of his record of bold and competent leadership.

25
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.239
Rick had a deep understanding

26
00:01:06.239 --> 00:01:08.680
of how cities and counties function,

27
00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.680
funding, growth, and quality of life.

28
00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.480
I appreciated his insight,

29
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.639
as I've learned more about this side of politics.

30
00:01:16.639 --> 00:01:19.760
I only had a handful of in-person conversations with Rick,

31
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.300
but I found them extremely valuable.

32
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.879
I had hoped to connect with him again

33
00:01:23.879 --> 00:01:27.080
after his election and swearing in as Nampa's mayor,

34
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.120
but I assumed there was no hurry,

35
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.019
that we had all the time in the world.

36
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.720
It's a tragic reminder that life can be short,

37
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.760
and none of us are guaranteed tomorrow.

38
00:01:38.319 --> 00:01:41.059
Rick first reached out to me a couple of years ago

39
00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:43.440
after reading some of my writing.

40
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.080
He was curious, not about political ideas,

41
00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.919
but about my Christian faith.

42
00:01:47.919 --> 00:01:49.199
His own faith was evident

43
00:01:49.199 --> 00:01:51.760
in every aspect of his life and work,

44
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.400
and I know of few better witnesses for Jesus Christ

45
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.319
in the political arena.

46
00:01:56.319 --> 00:01:59.239
Rick was everything citizens want in a public servant

47
00:01:59.239 --> 00:02:00.360
and elected leader.

48
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.680
He surely had a long career ahead of him,

49
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.680
but it was cut short far too soon.

50
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.839
Rick Hogoboam was a husband, father, pastor, and leader.

51
00:02:09.839 --> 00:02:12.080
His loss will be keenly felt across Idaho,

52
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:15.559
especially in Nampa, which has lost a young mayor.

53
00:02:15.559 --> 00:02:18.440
Above all, keep his wife and five children in your prayers

54
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.919
as they face this sudden tragedy.

55
00:02:20.919 --> 00:02:23.679
Above all, Rick demonstrated that it was possible

56
00:02:23.679 --> 00:02:25.179
to engage in the political arena

57
00:02:25.179 --> 00:02:27.979
without sacrificing your faith or your humanity.

58
00:02:29.039 --> 00:02:32.000
On the top of his Facebook page, he posted the verse,

59
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.839
for what shall it profit a man

60
00:02:33.839 --> 00:02:37.380
if he shall gain the whole world and lose his own soul?

61
00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:41.240
I rejoice that Rick never lost his soul.

62
00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.080
I hope this tragedy reminds us

63
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.399
to keep our priorities in order,

64
00:02:45.399 --> 00:02:47.220
to remember what truly matters

65
00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.500
in how we spend the limited time and energy

66
00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.839
we've been given.

67
00:02:51.559 --> 00:02:53.600
After all, none of us knows how long we have.

68
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.660
May his memory be an example to other public servants

69
00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.199
and a blessing to us all.

70
00:02:58.199 --> 00:02:59.600
About Brian Allman.

71
00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:03.679
Brian Allman is the editor of the Gem State Chronicle.

72
00:03:03.679 --> 00:03:05.160
He also serves as chairman

73
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.199
of the District 14 Republican Party

74
00:03:07.199 --> 00:03:10.000
and is a trustee of the Eagle Public Library Board.

75
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.559
He lives with his wife and five children in Eagle.

76
00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.860
Web, more posts, seven.
